From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: Send to, and Pin to Quick access

The item menu's Send to: the user's SendTo folder by name (shortcuts to
programs, which get the files as arguments, and to folders, which get a copy;
folders; programs; "Desktop (create shortcut)" (.DeskLink); "Documents"
(.mydocs); and any other type's "sendto" command, %* for the files -- how
sg-zip's "Compressed (zipped) Folder" (.ZFSendToTarget) is reached), then the
removable drives. "Pin to Quick access" / "Unpin from Quick access" for
folders (verbs pintohome and unpinfromhome), kept in
HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\Explorer\QuickAccess "Pinned", which File
Explorer shows.

Gate: test/explorer2-gate.sh.
